# Vulnerability details

## Impact
> Please note that this issue is also applicable to Singularity.addCollateral. Because we are unsure if this should be separate ticket and for brevity we have decided to lump these two issues into one ticket. The Singularity code is almost identical to Singularity.addCollateral. A hacker is able to bypass the Singularity allowedBorrow check by setting shares to 0 and amount to a value that is withdrawalable from the victim's account.  

BigBang.addCollateral allows hackers to bypass the borrow allowance check. Because of this, hackers can steal collateral from other users and add the collateral to their account.

This is because Tapioca allows users to provide both an amount and a share argument. If the share argument is 0, the amount argument is used as the share value. Unfortunately, the amount converted to shares is not checked to see if the spender is allowed to borrow those funds. This allows a hacker to bypass the allowedBorrow check.

