# Vulnerability details

## Impact

In the function `getDebtRate()`, `_currentDebt` is set to `totalBorrow.elastic`. This is the current total amount of debt users take in this market, so it can have any value. However, there is a calculation `_currentDebt - debtStartPoint`, but it does not check the case where `_currentDebt < debtStartPoint`, which could cause the transaction to revert.

Since `getDebtRate()` is called in `_accrue()`, which is called in every function, it will cause a Denial of Service (DOS) for all functionalities of the market and lock the assets in it.

## Proof of Concept

There is a check for `totalBorrow.elastic == 0`, but no check that it is smaller than `debtStartPoint`.
```solidity
function getDebtRate() public view returns (uint256) {
    if (_isEthMarket) return penrose.bigBangEthDebtRate(); // default 0.5%
    if (totalBorrow.elastic == 0) return minDebtRate;

    uint256 _ethMarketTotalDebt = BigBang(penrose.bigBangEthMarket())
        .getTotalDebt();
    uint256 _currentDebt = totalBorrow.elastic;
    uint256 _maxDebtPoint = (_ethMarketTotalDebt *
        debtRateAgainstEthMarket) / 1e18;

    if (_currentDebt >= _maxDebtPoint) return maxDebtRate;

    // @audit _currentDebt could be smaller than debtStartPoint
    uint256 debtPercentage = ((_currentDebt - debtStartPoint) * 
        DEBT_PRECISION) / (_maxDebtPoint - debtStartPoint);
    uint256 debt = ((maxDebtRate - minDebtRate) * debtPercentage) /
        DEBT_PRECISION +
        minDebtRate;

    if (debt > maxDebtRate) return maxDebtRate;

    return debt;
}
```

