# Vulnerability details

## Description

 The UniswapV3Swapper contract incorrectly calculates the amount out for amount in. The calculation is performed using the following formula:

amountOut = OracleLibrary.getQuoteAtTick(tick, uint128(amountIn), tokenIn, tokenOut)

However, the OracleLibrary.getQuoteAtTick() function does not take into account the pool fee. This means that the amount out will be overestimated, which could result in users losing funds.


## Impact
This bug could result in users losing funds if they expect to receive a certain amount of tokens after a swap, but the actual amount received is less due to the pool fee not being taken into account.


