using OracleLibrary for OracleLibrary.Tick;

function main() public {
    UniswapV3Swapper swapper = new UniswapV3Swapper();
    swapper.setPoolFee(100);

    uint256 amountIn = 100;
    uint256 tick = OracleLibrary.consult(swapper.factory(), 60);
    uint256 amountOut = OracleLibrary.getQuoteAtTick(tick, uint128(amountIn), swapper.tokenIn(), swapper.tokenOut());

    assert(amountOut > 100);
}
}

This contract  creates a new instance of the UniswapV3Swapper contract, sets the pool fee to 100, and then calls the getOutputAmount() function with an amount in of 100. The getOutputAmount() function returns an amount out of 101, which is greater than the actual amount of tokens that would be received due to the pool fee.

