## Description


The _repay function of the SGLLendingCommon contract does not check if the total borrow amount after the repayment is still below the borrow cap. This can lead to the borrow cap being exceeded, which can cause the contract to revert.

The following code shows the bug in the _repay function:

function _repay(
    address from,
    address to,
    bool skim,
    uint256 part
) internal returns (uint256 amount) {
    totalBorrow -= part;

    userBorrowPart[to] -= part;

    uint256 share = yieldBox.toShare(assetId, amount, true);
    uint128 totalShare = totalAsset.elastic;
    _addTokens(from, to, assetId, share, uint256(totalShare), skim);
    totalAsset.elastic = totalShare + uint128(share);
    emit LogRepay(skim ? address(yieldBox) : from, to, amount, part);
}
The totalBorrow variable tracks the total amount of borrows for the contract. The _repay function subtracts part from the totalBorrow variable, but it does not check if the total borrow amount after the repayment is still below the borrow cap. This means that it is possible for the totalBorrow variable to exceed the borrow cap after the _repay function is called.

## Impact 

If the totalBorrow variable exceeds the borrow cap, the _repay function will revert. This can prevent users from repaying their borrows, and it can also cause other problems for the contract.

