# Vulnerability details

## Impact
If a malicious user provides an extremely large `_duration` value, it can exceed the maximum value that can be safely represented by uint56 (56 bits). Consequently, this triggers an integer overflow during the conversion from `_duration` to `uint56`, leading to an unexpected and incorrect value for `expiry`. This can result in a situation where the user's participation never expires, effectively giving them perpetual voting power and rewards, and disrupting the fairness and integrity of the governance system.

