## Impact
If the `twTap.participate` function throws an exception (reverts), it will consume all the gas allocated for the current transaction. 

## Proof of Concept
The `try-catch` block is catching an error of type `Error`, but Solidity does not have a built-in `Error` type. Instead, Solidity uses `revert()` to handle exceptions, which causes the current transaction to revert and consume all remaining gas.

If the `twTap.participate` function throws an exception (reverts), it will consume all the gas allocated for the current transaction. This means that any remaining logic after the `try-catch` block won't be executed, and the state changes made before the function call may not be reverted.

